  "guideReadingStep3": "Use page arrows on the website, or swipe on a touch device to change pages. Your last-read position is saved automatically on this device.",
  "guideReadingTip": "The Quran remains Arabic when you change the interface language. You do not need an account to read.",
  "guideSearchTitle": "Search and save bookmarks",
  "guideSearchStep1": "Choose Search Quran on Home, or open Search in the reader. Enter a word or phrase from the Arabic Quran.",
  "guideSearchStep2": "Select a search result. The panel closes and opens the Mushaf at that Ayah automatically. Press and hold an Ayah to open its actions.",
  "guideSearchStep3": "Choose a bookmark color from the Ayah actions. Open Bookmarks to return to your saved Ayahs.",
  "guideSearchTip": "Search currently covers the Arabic Quran, not Tafsir or translations. Bookmarks use the existing yellow, red and green groups.",
  "guideLibraryTitle": "Choose Tafsir and translations",
  "guideLibraryStep1": "Open Library, then choose Tafsir or Translations.",
  "guideLibraryStep2": "Use Download for an additional resource, or Select for one already available. Wait for the ready confirmation.",
  "guideLibraryStep3": "Return to the Mushaf, press and hold an Ayah and open its Tafsir action to read the selected resource.",
  "guideLibraryTip": "Interface language and reading resource are independent. Saved resources can be read offline; browser storage must be available.",
  "guideAudioTitle": "Listen to recitations",
  "guideAudioStep1": "Open the reader audio controls to choose a reciter. Different controls may offer different reciter lists.",
  "guideAudioStep2": "In Library, choose Recitations, select a Surah and press Play. You can also play an Ayah from its actions in the Mushaf.",
  "guideAudioStep3": "Use the audio player to pause or continue. Resume listening returns to the saved audio position when one is available.",
  "guideAudioTip": "Online audio comes from external recitation providers. Download complete Surah recordings separately under Recitations for offline listening; word-by-word audio still needs internet.",
  "guideOfflineTitle": "Prepare before going offline",
  "guideOfflineStep1": "On the website, open Settings and choose Prepare offline reading. Keep the tab open until Ready for offline reading appears. The phone app includes the Mushaf.",
  "guideOfflineStep2": "In Library, download the Tafsir and translations you want while connected. Offline app preparation does not download these additional resources or audio.",
  "guideOfflineStep3": "In the phone app, choose a Surah under Library → Recitations and use Download for offline. Test your saved content without a connection before relying on it.",
  "guideOfflineTip": "Browsers may remove saved files when space is low. Private browsing is not suitable for lasting storage. App preparation, downloaded books and saved Surah recordings are separate downloads.",
  "guidePlansTitle": "Build a reading and memorization routine",
  "guidePlansStep1": "Open Plans → Khatmah. Create a plan, choose a completion period and start it. Mark the daily reading only after you finish it.",
  "guidePlansStep2": "Open Memorization and create a plan with a Surah, Ayah range, repetition count and delay.",
  "guidePlansStep3": "Play the range, hide or reveal the text, and mark Ayahs as memorized or for revision. Use the previous and next controls to move within your range.",
  "guidePlansTip": "Plan progress is saved on this device. Audio repetition still needs a playable source or a supported saved download.",
  "guideSettingsTitle": "Make the experience comfortable",
  "guideSettingsStep1": "In Settings → Language, choose العربية, English or Español. The guide and interface follow your choice.",
  "guideSettingsStep2": "In Settings → Appearance, choose light, dark or the system setting.",
  "guideSettingsStep3": "In the phone app, optionally enable a daily reminder, choose its time and grant notification permission.",
  "guideSettingsTip": "Daily reminder notifications are available on supported phones, not the website. You can turn them off again in Settings.",
  "guideStorageTitle": "Understand your local data",
  "guideStorageStep1": "Bookmarks, reading position, plans, preferences and saved downloads remain on this device or in this browser. There is no account or cross-device sync.",
  "guideStorageStep2": "Keep using the same browser profile to retain website data. Another device, browser or profile has its own separate data.",
  "guideStorageTip": "Clearing app/site data or losing the device can erase saved items. Use Local backup in Settings to export personal data privately; downloaded books and audio are not included.",
